<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss Telecom sees 2,000 job cuts in privatisation.</title>
<headline>Swiss Telecom sees 2,000 job cuts in privatisation.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1996-09-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>State agency Swiss Telecom PTT expects to cut 2,000 jobs or ten percent of its workforce in the next four years under plans for privatisation and market liberalisation in 1998, director Felix Rosenberg said.</p>
<p>Rosenberg told a Swiss weekly newspaper the cuts would come mainly in traditional telephone services and maintanence.</p>
<p>He said the reduction could be carried out without redundancies by using early retirement, normal employee turnover and by retraining staff for new jobs in growing areas of the telecoms agency.</p>
</text>
